# Political Triumph under Innkeeper's Talent at level 3 ("put twice that many of each of those kinds of counters instead",
# CR 614.1a): the plan counters a trigger puts are two, put at once. Its first plan counter is put on turn 1 before the
# Talent reaches level 3, so the count goes 1, then 3 on turn 3, then 5 on turn 5: the fourth counter is among the two put
# by the third Ornithopter's trigger, so "when the fourth plan counter is put" triggers, and only once for that event
# (CR 603.2c) - the fifth counter triggers nothing more. Bot1 draws one card (the Plains), and each Ornithopter gets two
# +1/+1 counters from it (doubled too), beside those the Talent's level-1 combat trigger put on turns 1 and 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Political Triumph
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Innkeeper's Talent
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

